*** OperServ Operator Help - Command: OPER ***
Manages the services access lists.
 
Syntax: OPER ADD nick level
        OPER DEL nick
        OPER INFO nick
        OPER SET nick ENABLED YES|NO
        OPER SET nick AKILLPROXY YES|NO
        OPER LIST [level]
 
ADD adds the given nick with the given level, which can
be one of HOP/SOP/SA/SRA/CODER. If a nick is already on a
list, it will be raised/demoted to the new list accordingly.
 
Note: All entries must be enabled after being added
in order to work.
 
AKILLPROXY marks an entry as a network proxy monitor.
Akills it adds are typed as proxy akills and show up as
such in AKILL LIST, AKILL INFO and in the akill ID, so
that they can be told apart from the ones an oper added
by hand. An oper cannot grant this to his own entry.
 
This command is limited to Services Administrators.
